        // Page Content
        .container-fluid.p-0

            // About
            section#about.resume-section
                .resume-section-content
                    h1.mb-0
                        | Victor Soto 
                        span.text-primary Alexander
                    .subheading.mb-5
                        | Mexico City · (+52) 55-6676-9310 ·
                        a(href='mailto:alexandervictor550@gmail.com') alexandervictor550@gmail.com
                    p.lead.mb-5
                        | System Development Engineer focused on backend automation and operational tooling for large-scale publishing systems on AWS — building AI-assisted workflows and self-serve diagnostics in Java and Python that eliminate manual effort and reduce incident load. Hands-on with core AWS services (S3, DynamoDB, Lambda, CloudWatch, Athena) and an AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner. Quantitative engineering background (geophysics / signal processing) with strong fundamentals in data, noisy systems, and building reliable, maintainable solutions.
                    .mb-5
                        a.btn.btn-primary(href='assets/pdf/Victor_Soto_Alexander_CV.pdf', target='_blank')
                            i.fas.fa-download.me-2
                            | Download CV (PDF)
                    .social-icons
                        a.social-icon(href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/soto-alexander/' target='_blank')
                            i.fab.fa-linkedin-in
                        a.social-icon(href='https://github.com/victoralexander132' target='_blank')
                            i.fab.fa-github

            hr.m-0

            // Experience
            section#experience.resume-section
               .resume-section-content
                    h2.mb-5 Experience

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 System Development Engineer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Amazon · promoted from Support Engineer III
                            p Automation- and tooling-focused engineer on the KDP/POD publisher-support organization, building systems that reduce operational load across the team.
                            ul
                                li Built an autonomous AI agent that scans publisher content-eligibility tickets daily and resolves them without supervision, auto-resolving ~90% and cutting handling time from 30–90 minutes of manual triage to 5–10 minutes of review.
                                li Automated a manual financial-reporting process covering hundreds of thousands of publishers and records across Amazon's global publishing pipeline, saving ~20 engineer-hours per month via scripted and AI-assisted workflows.
                                li Codified resolution logic for ~10 recurring failure modes into self-serve automation, cutting missed SLAs by 60% and reducing manual escalations.
                                li Designed a Git-backed documentation-as-code pipeline that made SOPs peer-reviewable and directly consumable by AI agents.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary June 2026 - Present

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Support Engineer III
                            .subheading.mb-3 Amazon
                            p Sustained the reliability of publisher-reporting infrastructure while building automation to shrink the team's operational burden.
                            ul
                                li Resolved ~1,400 production trouble tickets over 29 months across 4 resolver groups, maintaining 90%+ SLA compliance.
                                li Owned on-call for the Kindle publisher-reporting backend, resolving 90%+ of pages without escalation.
                                li Cut repeat self-service marketing tickets ~60% (and recurring tickets ~40% overall) by closing documentation gaps and assigning explicit content ownership.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary January 2024 - June 2026

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Software Engineer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Unosquare
                            p Built and maintained software solutions for US-based clients using Java and SQL databases in a Scrum / continuous-delivery workflow.
                            ul
                                li Managed database schema changes using SQL, ensuring data consistency across multiple systems.
                                li Built and maintained API test suites for RESTful services using ReadyAPI.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary August 2022 - December 2023

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Geophysical Engineer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Geoexplora
                            p Automated seismic data-processing workflows with Bash scripting, improving turnaround and accuracy on large datasets.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary August 2019 - February 2022

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Junior Java Fullstack Developer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Generation Mexico
                            p Completed an intensive, hands-on Java fullstack bootcamp — building and testing web applications with Java and Spring Boot, designing relational databases with MySQL, and implementing front-end interfaces with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary March 2022 - June 2022

